message.content:
To expose runtime metrics to the client HUD in a protocol-first way while maintaining simulation authority in the runtime, we need to:

1.  **Extend the Protocol**: Add a new `runtime.metrics` server message type to `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`.
2.  **Update Runtime Server**: Modify `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts` to include metrics in the `session.state` payload and emit a dedicated `runtime.metrics` message when metrics change.
3.  **Update Client**: Modify `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx` to consume the new metrics and display them in the HUD.
4.  **Add Contract Tests**: Add tests to `apps/game-runtime/test/ui-contract.integration.test.ts` to verify the new message structure.

Here is the minimal change set:

### 1. Extend Protocol (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`)

Add the `RuntimeMetrics` type and the `runtime.metrics` server message variant.

```typescript
// packages/protocol/src/messages.ts

// ... existing imports

export type RuntimeMetrics = {
  turnsTotal: number;
  invalidOutputCount: number;
  actionAppliedCount: number;
  actionRejectedCount: number;
  queuedActions: number;
};

// ... existing types

export type ServerMessage =
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "session.state";
      payload: {
        phase: SessionPhase;
        paused: boolean;
        preparedSeed: number | null;
        threadIds: { gameplayByAgentId: Record<string, string>; builder?: string };
        connected: boolean;
        runtime: {
          model: string | null;
          effort: TurnEffort;
          tickMs: number;
          schedulerMs: number;
          maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: number;
          availableModels: RuntimeModelOption[];
          metrics?: RuntimeMetrics; // Add metrics here for initial state
        };
      };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "runtime.metrics"; // New message type
      payload: RuntimeMetrics;
    }
  // ... rest of ServerMessage union
```

### 2. Update Runtime Server (`apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`)

Update `sendSessionState` to include metrics and emit `runtime.metrics` whenever metrics change.

```typescript
// apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts

// ... existing imports

// Inside GameRuntimeServer class:

private sendSessionState(): void {
  const metrics = this.metrics.snapshot();
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "session.state",
    payload: {
      phase: this.phase,
      paused: this.paused,
      preparedSeed: this.preparedSeed,
      threadIds: this.threadIds,
      connected: this.connected,
      runtime: {
        model: this.turnModel,
        effort: this.turnEffort,
        tickMs: runtimeConfig.tickMs,
        schedulerMs: runtimeConfig.schedulerMs,
        maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: runtimeConfig.maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn,
        availableModels: this.availableModels,
        metrics // Include current metrics
      }
    }
  });
}

// Update tick() to emit metrics on change
private tick(): void {
  // ... existing logic ...

  // After updating metrics in tick logic
  this.metrics.setQueueDepth(this.totalQueuedActions());

  // Emit metrics update if anything changed (simplified: always emit on tick for HUD sync)
  // In a more optimized version, we could diff, but for HUD sync, sending on tick is safe.
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: this.metrics.snapshot()
  });

  this.sendWorldSnapshot();
}

// Update requestGameplayTurn to emit metrics after turn completion
private async requestGameplayTurn(agentId: string, isRetry: boolean, previousText: string): Promise<void> {
  // ... existing logic ...

  this.metrics.onTurnCompleted();

  // Emit metrics update
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: this.metrics.snapshot()
  });

  // ... rest of logic ...
}

// Update resetSession to reset and emit metrics
private async resetSession(seed?: number): Promise<void> {
  // ... existing logic ...
  this.metrics.setQueueDepth(0);

  // Emit reset metrics
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: this.metrics.snapshot()
  });

  // ... rest of logic ...
}
```

### 3. Update Client (`apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`)

Add state for metrics and update the HUD to display them.

```typescript
